   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cost of operating West Kalimantan power system reduced</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In West Kalimantan, PLN&apos;s average cost of generation reduced to $0.18/kWh (2009 baseline: $0.25/kWh) 
Achievement: 0.07 
Progress/Status: As of 30 September 2020, West Kalimantan (Khatulistiwa System, interconnected with SESCO) average cost of generation is IDR 1,105/kWh (from IDR 1,142/kWh in July 2020) = $0.07/kWh (ADB exchange rate as of 30 September 2020, USD 1 = IDR14,869).  The decrease in generation cost is because the costly diesel power plants are gradually decreased by end of 2018, West Kalimantan mainly relies on coal and imported energy from Sarawak 
Data Source: Electricity statistics published by PLN</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2011"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="0.18"></target>
     <actual value="0.07"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Power interconnection capacity of 230  MW established 
Achievement: 208.8 
Progress/Status: &#x2022;	As of 30 September 2020, average actual power import is 159.93MW during off-peak hours and 208.76MW during peak hours. Average power import reached 230MW up to 245.4 MW (peak hours) from October 2017 to May 2020.
&#x2022;	5th Amendment of PEA will be signed in December 2020 and applied in 2021. It regulates electricity purchase from SESCO with nominated capacity of peak/off-peak hours 110/80 MW. 
&#x2022;	Coal power plant projects from previous government&apos;s electricity generation Fast Tack Program (FTP) 1 and FTP2 are now completed or being constructed. The price of coal is IDR 900/kWh, while the import price is MYR 32.32 cent/kWh (IDR 1,156/kWh, based on ADB forex as of 30 September 2020). This reduces the need of imported power.
&#x2022;	Future power import targets are decreased in PEA and RUPTL 2018-2027. The interconnected grid will continue to contribute in ensuring Khatulistiwa grid reliability and stability, with potential two-way power purchase agreements (export and import) to Sarawak. Based on RUPTL 2019-2028, the Khatulistiwa grid is planned to be interconnected to Barito Mahakam grid of Central/South Kalimantan. 
Data Source: PLN&apos;s Annual Reports</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2011"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="230"></target>
     <actual value="208.8"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
